---
description: The agent that implements a change does not review it
alwaysApply: true
---

- Do not review your own change.
- Hand UX, architecture, security, tests, performance, and code quality to the
  readonly agents: ux-reviewer, architect, security-reviewer, test-engineer,
  performance-reviewer, and code-reviewer.
- Find failures before suggesting improvements.
- Do not set Status to accepted on an intent, experience, spec, plan, ADR,
  architecture gate, orchestration log, or debt record.
- The orchestrator may sequence roles and must not be the builder or the approver.
